invariant: INV-17
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: rsa_sign_equiv_test
reason: rsa_sign64_sp1 returns without wiping s, the limbs of the
  candidate it recombined. After a check that passed they are the
  signature the caller holds. A candidate that failed its check differs
  from the signature modulo one prime alone, and it and the message
  factor the modulus. bin/rsa_sign_equiv_test signs under a key with one
  bit of dp changed, copies the stack below the refused call and finds
  the candidate's limbs there.

--- old
    ct_wipe(m2, sizeof m2);
    ct_wipe(s, sizeof s);
--- new
    ct_wipe(m2, sizeof m2);
